<title>USA: Industrial Q3 shr loss $0.29 with SAIF.</title>
<headline>Industrial Q3 shr loss $0.29 with SAIF.</headline>
<dateline>BELLEVUE, Ohio 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended</p>
<p>						  9/30/96	   9/30/95</p>
<p>FINANCIAL RATIOS</p>
<p> Return on average assets		 (1.85)%	     1.55%</p>
<p> Return on average equity		  (9.57)		7.98</p>
<p>Average equity to</p>
<p>   average assets			     19.28	     19.41</p>
<p> Net interest margin			   4.29		4.22</p>
<p> Interest rate spread			  3.32		3.33</p>
<p>Operating expenses</p>
<p>   to average assets			   6.04		1.86</p>
<p>SHARE DATA</p>
<p> Book value per share			$10.92	    $14.46</p>
<p> Earnings per share (a)		     (.29)		 .17</p>
<p>							  Nine months ended</p>
<p>						  9/30/96	   9/30/95</p>
<p>FINANCIAL RATIOS</p>
<p> Return on average assets		   0.43%	     1.35%</p>
<p> Return on average equity		    2.05		9.04</p>
<p>Average equity to</p>
<p>   average assets			     21.10	     14.89</p>
<p> Net interest margin			   4.39		3.94</p>
<p> Interest rate spread			  3.29		3.30</p>
<p>Operating expenses</p>
<p>   to average assets			   3.37		1.87</p>
<p> Earnings per share (a)		     $ .20	     $ .17</p>
<p>(a)  1995 earnings per share was computed based upon weighted average shares outstanding and net income subsequent to the stock conversion on August 1, 1995.</p>
<p>Net income was a $1.5 million loss for the quarter and a profit of $1 million for the nine-month period. The net income figures include a pre-tax charge of $1.5 million for recapitalizing the Savings Association Insurance Fund.  </p>
<p>Total assets at September 30 were $320.4 million, compared to $309.3 million reported a year ago. Total loans, net of the allowance for loan losses, increased $25.3 million to $277.3 million at September 30, from $252.0 million a year ago. Non-performing loans as a percentage of total loans fell from 0.53 percent a year ago to 0.52 percent at September 30.</p>
